// F. SIZES, ROUND TRIP, RUN TIME
row('round/bevel with size 0 or a negative size; round(shape, 0)', 'refused',
  `${CMD} ids sz-* (cases-r2.mjs), e-zero-size etc. The interpreter only checks that the size is a number. ${P(['sz-edge-round-0', 'sz-edge-round-neg', 'sz-edge-bevel-0', 'sz-edge-bevel-neg', 'e-zero-size', 'e-neg-size', 'e-bevel-zero', 'e-bevel-neg', 'n-e-fillet-r1e-6', 'n-e-bevel-d1e-6', 'n-e-fillet-r0.001', 'sz-whole-round-0', 'sz-whole-round-neg'], { terse: true })} A size of 1e-6 (positive) is also refused with "fillet size must be positive" - misleading wording; 0.001 builds (pane 14400.0 = rig). Sentence (pane): "${paneSent('sz-edge-round-0')}" / "${paneSent('sz-edge-bevel-neg')}" - it names the size ("must be positive"), so it is the real cause. The RIG showed "no edge at [x, y, z]: the nearest edge is 6.366 mm away" instead (rig artifact). round(b, 0) is SILENT and correct: ${m('sz-whole-round-0')} (an unrounded box, no message). round(b, -2): ${m('sz-whole-round-neg', { cf: false })}; kernel: "solid.fillet: invalid input: fillet size must be positive". Non-number: "${ALL['sz-edge-round-nan']?.interp?.errors?.[0]}" (plain). ${NOTPLAIN}(prefix "solidcraft refused it -- solid.fillet:"); no interpreter sentence for 0 or negative.`,
  paneSent('sz-edge-round-0') ?? sentenceOf('sz-edge-round-0'));
{
  const rtl = (label) => RT.find((x) => x.label === label);
  row('toScript() round trip of blend features (doc -> script text -> doc)', 'wrong',
    `cmd: bun contract/fillet-chamfer-evidence/roundtrip.mjs > roundtrip-results.json (no kernel). roundStyle CHAMFER on a primitive does NOT round-trip: toScript({box, round 4, roundStyle chamfer}) emits ${JSON.stringify(rtl('box roundStyle chamfer').emitted)} and re-running it gives roundStyle ${rtl('box roundStyle chamfer').diff.after[0].roundStyle} (a chamfered part silently becomes a filleted part after save and reopen); same for a cylinder (${JSON.stringify(rtl('cylinder roundStyle chamfer').emitted)}). Fillet style, corner:3 (re-emitted as round(box1, 3); the doc only gains an explicit roundStyle:'fillet'), edge blends (written as fillet()/chamfer(), re-run the same), alias forms and pocket-wall edges survive (feature ids are renumbered pocket1 -> op1, harmless). STRUCTURE IS LOST: a hand-built list round([e1, e2], 2) re-emits as two fillet() lines, and a pocket rim re-emits as four separate fillet(pocket1.edge('top', pocket1.wall(sk1, n))) lines, so any batching must be done on consecutive same-size blends, not on the list/rim syntax. roundStyle chamfer is reachable only from ModelDoc (script text cannot set it) but save/load goes through toScript.`);
}
{
  const p = (id) => (PERF[id] ? `${id}: ${PERF[id].times.join(' / ')} ms (3 repeats, isolated)` : `${id}: ${ALL[id]?.fx?.ms} ms`);
  row('bounded run time with a sentence for slow blend builds (no timeout, no progress, no sentence today)', 'unsupported',
    `${CMD} ids pf-* (cases-r2.mjs), perf.mjs (the exact command lists the translator emitted, 3 repeats, nothing else running). ${['pf-cyl-whole-r3', 'pf-cyl-offc-whole-r3', 'pf-corner-then-join', 'ov-d-box-fillet-4', 'ov-d-box-fillet-9.99', 'ov-f-pair-cyl-10', 'ov-c-cyl-single-14.9'].map(p).join('; ')}. The slow ones are correct (whole cylinder round r3 matches OCCT = closed form to 4.0e-5; round-then-join of two corner-rounded boxes 27251.3577 vs OCCT 27251.6365, 1.0e-5, 60 vs 64 faces) but take ten seconds to ~2 minutes with the page busy and no timeout or message (the critic measured 12 s and 86 s; the machine was shared with other builds, so timings vary by about 2x). Nothing in the product bounds the time or tells the student; unsupported until it does.`);
}

